Phase OS-19: Kernel Scheduler Enhancements - 3 new AArch64 assembly kernel modules:

1. kernel/sched_rt.asm (Real-Time Scheduling)
   - Base ID: 919
   - Real-time task scheduling with priority-based policies
   - Features: SCHED_FIFO and SCHED_RR policies, priority inheritance, deadline scheduling, real-time bandwidth control, priority boosting, RT throttling prevention
   - Data structures: rt_task_t (task_id, rt_priority, policy, runtime, deadline, period), rt_queue_t (priority_level, task_count, head, tail)
   - API: sched_rt_init, sched_rt_register(task_id, priority, policy), sched_rt_unregister(task_id), sched_rt_set_priority(task_id, priority), sched_rt_set_deadline(task_id, runtime, deadline, period), sched_rt_next_task() => task_id, sched_rt_stats(out_stats)
   - Capacity: 64 RT tasks, 100 priority levels (0-99), 2 policies (FIFO, RR)
   - Pattern: follow kernel/memory.asm style (stp/ldp frame, .global exports, .bss for state)

2. kernel/sched_cgroup.asm (Control Groups)
   - Base ID: 920
   - Control group management for resource allocation and isolation
   - Features: cgroup hierarchy, CPU/memory/IO resource limits, task assignment, usage tracking, cgroup creation/deletion, resource statistics
   - Data structures: cgroup_t (group_id, parent_id, name, cpu_shares, mem_limit, io_limit, task_count), cgroup_stats_t (cpu_usage, mem_usage, io_usage)
   - API: sched_cgroup_init, sched_cgroup_create(name, parent_id) => group_id, sched_cgroup_delete(group_id), sched_cgroup_add_task(group_id, task_id), sched_cgroup_remove_task(group_id, task_id), sched_cgroup_set_limits(group_id, cpu, mem, io), sched_cgroup_stats(group_id, out_stats)
   - Capacity: 32 cgroups, 1024 task assignments, hierarchical depth 8
   - Pattern: follow kernel/memory.asm style

3. kernel/sched_workqueue.asm (Work Queue Management)
   - Base ID: 921
   - Deferred work execution via work queues
   - Features: work queue creation, work item scheduling, delayed work execution, work cancellation, flush operations, worker thread management, work statistics
   - Data structures: workqueue_t (queue_id, name, max_workers, pending_count, active_count), work_item_t (work_id, func_ptr, data, delay_ms, state, queue_id)
   - API: sched_workqueue_init, sched_workqueue_create(name, max_workers) => queue_id, sched_workqueue_submit(queue_id, func, data) => work_id, sched_workqueue_submit_delayed(queue_id, func, data, delay_ms) => work_id, sched_workqueue_cancel(work_id), sched_workqueue_flush(queue_id), sched_workqueue_destroy(queue_id), sched_workqueue_stats(queue_id, out_stats)
   - Capacity: 16 work queues, 256 pending work items, 64 worker threads
   - Pattern: follow kernel/memory.asm style

Build all 3 kernel modules with:
  clang --target=aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu -c -O2 -o kernel/<name>.o kernel/<name>.asm

